# BL-82 EM-5.16 item D (BL-20 feats) — Diary Feats-tab node names + tooltips.
# Ported verbatim from docs/design/lore/chargen/30-feats.md (Provenance
# bookkeeping stripped). One message per FeatSkill variant; VALUE = title,
# .desc = tooltip description. Keep in sync with skill_i18n.rs's match arms.
hud-feat-athlete_title = Athlete
    .desc = The character's body is honed to move at the edge of mortal capability: they rise from prone with a single foot of movement, can run and jump with only the shortest wind-up, and climb at full speed without hesitation.
hud-feat-charger_title = Charger
    .desc = After rushing across open ground, the character crashes into a foe with overwhelming momentum — trading a careful step for a punishing strike or a shove that sends enemies stumbling backward.
hud-feat-crusher_title = Crusher
    .desc = The character's bludgeoning blows land with enough force to knock a foe off-balance, buying a split second in which every ally around them can press the advantage.
hud-feat-crossbow_expert_title = Crossbow Expert
    .desc = The character reloads and fires a hand crossbow with one-handed ease, ignoring the jostling of melee and putting bolts into enemies at point-blank range without penalty.
hud-feat-defensive_duelist_title = Defensive Duelist
    .desc = The character reads an incoming blow and deflects it with their own blade at the last instant, turning a potential wound into a near-miss through sheer timing.
hud-feat-dual_wielder_title = Dual Wielder
    .desc = The character fights with a weapon in each hand as a seamless whole, protecting themselves and striking faster than an opponent expects from someone carrying two blades.
hud-feat-great_weapon_master_title = Great Weapon Master
    .desc = The character channels the raw weight of a two-handed weapon into devastating follow-through attacks, accepting momentary recklessness for a killing blow that can drop opponents in a single swing.
hud-feat-heavy_armor_master_title = Heavy Armor Master
    .desc = The character's mastery of heavy plate allows them to shed minor blows outright, and their frame grows powerful enough to absorb punishment that would cripple a lightly armored fighter.
hud-feat-mage_slayer_title = Mage Slayer
    .desc = The character has spent enough time on battlefields where spellcasters decide the outcome to know how to disrupt a casting: punishing anyone who tries to shape a spell within reach, and resisting the magic that does land.
hud-feat-mobile_title = Mobile
    .desc = The character is a blur in combat — faster than most, able to charge through difficult terrain without cost, and impossible to punish with an opportunity attack after they strike.
hud-feat-piercer_title = Piercer
    .desc = The character's thrusting attacks find gaps in armor with clinical precision, letting them reroll a weak hit once and push the most critical strikes to maximum damage.
hud-feat-polearm_master_title = Polearm Master
    .desc = The character uses the full reach of a halberd, glaive, or spear — keeping enemies at bay with the butt of the weapon and striking before a foe can close the distance.
hud-feat-savage_attacker_title = Savage Attacker
    .desc = Once per turn the character can roll their damage dice twice and take the better result, turning a solid hit into something an opponent will remember — or not.
hud-feat-sentinel_title = Sentinel
    .desc = The character stands as an immovable wall: when an enemy tries to leave their reach, the character cuts them down, and when a foe attacks anyone nearby, the character punishes the distraction.
hud-feat-sharpshooter_title = Sharpshooter
    .desc = The character fires at range with ruthless efficiency — ignoring cover, sending bolts and arrows across improbable distances, and trading a measure of accuracy for shots that punch through even heavy protection.
hud-feat-shield_master_title = Shield Master
    .desc = The character uses their shield as both weapon and wall, shoving enemies aside with it as a bonus action and throwing themselves behind it to deflect magical blasts.
hud-feat-slasher_title = Slasher
    .desc = The character's slashing blows leave opponents slowed and off-balance, and a critical cut reduces the target's ability to strike back with full effectiveness.
hud-feat-speedy_title = Speedy
    .desc = The character moves with uncommon swiftness — they can dash as a bonus action and are harder to slow or stop, slipping out of difficult terrain and shaking off speed-reducing effects.
hud-feat-tavern_brawler_title = Tavern Brawler
    .desc = The character fights dirty and improvises constantly — broken bottles, kicked stools, headbutts — and can attempt to grapple an enemy as a bonus action after any unarmed strike lands.
hud-feat-aberrant_bloodmark_title = Aberrant Bloodmark
    .desc = A wild and uncontrolled bloodline power erupts in the character, granting a dangerous cantrip and a first-level spell that can misfire — a gift that is also a burden, setting them apart from those who bear cleaner marks.
hud-feat-arcane_college_initiate_title = Arcane College Initiate
    .desc = The character studies at one of the great arcane colleges, gaining two cantrips and a first-level spell from the curriculum of their chosen school.
hud-feat-artificer_initiate_title = Artificer Initiate
    .desc = The character picks up the basics of forge-craft enchantment: a cantrip and a first-level spell from the Artificer list, plus proficiency with one artisan's tool to channel that arcane work.
hud-feat-elemental_adept_title = Elemental Adept
    .desc = The character has drilled so deeply into one element — fire, cold, lightning, acid, or thunder — that their spells of that type pierce resistances and never roll the weakest possible damage.
hud-feat-frost_caster_title = Frost Caster
    .desc = The character's cold magic bites deeper than normal: they treat cold damage as if it pierces resistance, and targets they chill are slowed on their next turn.
hud-feat-genie_magic_title = Genie Magic
    .desc = The character's bloodline carries a trace of elemental heritage — they gain a selection of spells tied to one genie type and can use them once per long rest without a slot.
hud-feat-gift_of_the_chromatic_dragon_title = Gift of the Chromatic Dragon
    .desc = A draconic infusion tied to the primal chromatic lines grants the character a shimmering resistance to one energy type and the ability to lace a weapon strike once per day with elemental fury.
hud-feat-gift_of_the_gem_dragon_title = Gift of the Gem Dragon
    .desc = The crystalline thought-resonance of gem dragons grants the character a psychic retort — when struck, they can hurl their attacker backward with a burst of telekinetic force.
hud-feat-gift_of_the_metallic_dragon_title = Gift of the Metallic Dragon
    .desc = The protective nature of the metallic draconic line bleeds into the character: they can breathe a protective aura over an ally to grant temporary hit points, and resist one of the classic metallic breath-weapon energies.
hud-feat-greater_aberrant_bloodmark_title = Greater Aberrant Bloodmark
    .desc = The wild bloodline power deepens and steadies, granting the character an additional spell and expanding the unpredictable gift into something more controllable — though never fully tame.
hud-feat-magic_initiate_title = Magic Initiate
    .desc = The character dips into the well of another tradition, learning two cantrips and one low-level spell from a class list not their own — a minor but permanent gift of the arcane.
hud-feat-mythal_touched_title = Mythal Touched
    .desc = The character has been permanently altered by contact with a mythals weave — one of the great standing enchantments laid down in ancient times — gaining a lasting magical boon from the weave's residual power.
hud-feat-spell_sniper_title = Spell Sniper
    .desc = The character's attack spells reach twice as far as normal, cut through half and three-quarters cover, and add a cantrip from any tradition to their permanent repertoire.
hud-feat-spellfire_adept_title = Spellfire Adept
    .desc = The spellfire within the character has been trained into something coherent — they can absorb incoming spells to fuel devastating blasts of raw arcane energy.
hud-feat-spellfire_spark_title = Spellfire Spark
    .desc = The character has been touched by spellfire — a wild, unpredictable energy that courses through very few living beings — granting a minor channeling of raw arcane force.
hud-feat-telekinetic_title = Telekinetic
    .desc = The character learns to push objects and enemies with invisible force — a minor shove that can reposition allies and enemies alike, and a cantrip that moves things without touching them.
hud-feat-telepathic_title = Telepathic
    .desc = The character can speak mind-to-mind with any creature within reach of thought, and learn to probe a willing or sleeping mind for surface impressions without formal spellcasting.
hud-feat-umbra_touched_title = Umbra-Touched
    .desc = A brush with the deeper shadow of Umbriel marks the character permanently: they gain a point of ability score improvement, a single casting of Invisibility, and a first-level illusion or necromancy spell they can cast once per long rest without a slot.
hud-feat-veil_touched_title = Veil-Touched
    .desc = Something in the character has been brushed by the dream-thin membrane between the Material and the liminal fey realm: they gain a point of ability score improvement, a single casting of Misty Step, and a first-level enchantment or divination spell they can cast once per long rest without a slot.
hud-feat-war_caster_title = War Caster
    .desc = The character casts without dropping their weapon or shield, holds their concentration in the heat of combat through sheer will, and can hurl an opportunity-attack spell at an enemy who tries to slip away.
hud-feat-fairy_trickster_title = Fairy Trickster
    .desc = The character's blood carries a trace of minor fey mischief — they gain illusion and enchantment cantrips and a once-per-day ability to vanish in a puff of sparkling distraction.
hud-feat-inspiring_leader_title = Inspiring Leader
    .desc = The character delivers a rousing word before battle, granting every nearby ally temporary hit points drawn from their force of personality — a buffer that costs only a few minutes of speaking.
hud-feat-lordly_resolve_title = Lordly Resolve
    .desc = The character has absorbed the iron self-possession of those who rule — they gain resistance to psychic damage and can shake off fear and charm effects with an act of sheer will.
hud-feat-tireless_reveler_title = Tireless Reveler
    .desc = The character has trained their body and spirit to party without limit — they need less rest, recover morale faster, and can keep social situations alive through sheer infectious energy.
hud-feat-alert_title = Alert
    .desc = The character never lets their guard down; they cannot be surprised while conscious, add a bonus to initiative, and deny hidden enemies the advantage that comes from striking unseen.
hud-feat-chef_title = Chef
    .desc = The character cooks nutritious, morale-boosting food during rests: short-rest cooking produces temporary hit points for those who eat, and long-rest cooking allows allies to recover additional hit points on waking.
hud-feat-child_of_the_sun_title = Child of the Sun
    .desc = The character draws power from light itself — they generate their own luminance, and their attacks carry a burst of radiant warmth that damages creatures of darkness.
hud-feat-dungeon_delver_title = Dungeon Delver
    .desc = Years in ruins and catacombs have sharpened the character's instincts: they notice secret doors other explorers walk past, resist the traps built into ancient places, and move cautiously through hazardous terrain without triggering pressure plates.
hud-feat-healer_title = Healer
    .desc = The character's knowledge of wound care is good enough to stabilize a dying ally without a spell, and using a healer's kit they can restore hit points directly — more than a night's rest from a single pouch of bandages and herbs.
hud-feat-observant_title = Observant
    .desc = The character reads lips, misses nothing in a room, and carries a persistent bonus to passive Perception and Investigation that means they are rarely caught off-guard by what a scene contains.
hud-feat-shadowmoor_hexer_title = Shadowmoor Hexer
    .desc = The character has absorbed a fragment of deep shadow-lore, granting them the ability to lay curses on enemies — marks that make the target easier to hit and harder to protect.
hud-feat-bombardier_title = Bombardier
    .desc = The character becomes expert in the craft of alchemical grenades and explosive charges, increasing the blast radius and precision of any bomb they throw and gaining the ability to produce simple explosive devices during a short rest.
hud-feat-draconic_cult_initiate_title = Draconic Cult Initiate
    .desc = The character has been initiated into a secret order that venerates dragons as superior beings worthy of service, gaining a ritual draconic language and the ability to sense the presence of dragons nearby.
hud-feat-dragonscarred_title = Dragonscarred
    .desc = The character has survived a rite of intentional draconic wounding — the scars carry a fragment of the dragon's essence, granting elemental resistance and the ability to channel that same energy in a damaging burst.
hud-feat-orders_resilience_title = Order's Resilience
    .desc = The character's training in the order has tempered their endurance to iron — they gain advantage on Constitution saving throws and can shrug off exhaustion more readily than an untrained soldier.
hud-feat-poisoner_title = Poisoner
    .desc = The character ignores the risk of accidental poisoning, crafts contact and ingested toxins cheaply during short rests, and applies poison to a blade as a bonus action — a tradecraft that keeps enemies weak and off-balance.
hud-feat-quicksmith_title = Quicksmith
    .desc = The character can jury-rig a simple arcane device from available materials in a short rest — a basic focus, a mechanical lock, or a short-duration tool that functions until the next dawn.
hud-feat-strike_of_the_giants_title = Strike of the Giants
    .desc = The character has learned to channel the primal might of giants into their weapon strikes, choosing one giant type whose elemental power suffuses each powerful blow.
hud-feat-vampire_hunter_title = Vampire Hunter
    .desc = The character has devoted themselves to hunting the undead and in particular those who prey on the living by night — they gain expertise in identifying vampire signs and enhanced combat effectiveness against the creatures of blood.
hud-feat-bloodlust_title = Bloodlust
    .desc = A consuming hunger for violence lives in the character — when they reduce a creature to zero hit points, they can make a bonus attack, and their damage increases when they have been wounded.
hud-feat-cloying_mists_title = Cloying Mists
    .desc = The character can exhale or summon a clinging fog of unnatural origin that obscures their movements and disorients those who breathe it in.
hud-feat-delicious_pain_title = Delicious Pain
    .desc = Pain becomes fuel — when the character takes damage, they gain a burst of savage clarity that sharpens their next attack to a lethal edge.
hud-feat-durable_title = Durable
    .desc = The character's Constitution improves, and they recover more hit points every time they roll Hit Dice during a short rest — their body knits faster and more completely than anyone has a right to expect.
hud-feat-light_bringer_title = Light Bringer
    .desc = The character channels radiant energy as a weapon against darkness — they can produce a burst of searing light that harms undead and fiends specifically, and can maintain a persistent glow that denies shadow creatures concealment.
hud-feat-love_bites_title = Love Bites
    .desc = The character's touch carries a supernatural charm — a bite or close contact can fascinate a target, locking them in place while the character acts unimpeded.
hud-feat-lucky_title = Lucky
    .desc = The character has an uncanny gift for being in the right place at the right time: three times per day they can retroactively tip the scales — rerolling any die that affects them and choosing which result stands.
hud-feat-putrefy_title = Putrefy
    .desc = The character can channel necrotic rot into a touch or a wound, causing it to spread and weaken the target's ability to heal for a short time.
hud-feat-rebuke_title = Rebuke
    .desc = When the character is struck, they can unleash a punishing wave of energy that drives the attacker back and leaves them staggered.
hud-feat-resilient_title = Resilient
    .desc = The character strengthens one ability score and gains saving throw proficiency for that ability — closing a gap in their defenses by sheer disciplined practice.
hud-feat-tough_title = Tough
    .desc = The character's maximum hit points increase by two for every level they have and will gain — a permanent expansion of the raw capacity to absorb punishment before going down.
hud-feat-treacherous_allure_title = Treacherous Allure
    .desc = The character can project a supernaturally compelling presence that makes targets want to approach them and lowers resistance to their commands or suggestions.
hud-feat-vampire_touched_title = Vampire Touched
    .desc = The character has been changed by a deep vampiric influence — not full undeath, but a liminal state that grants darkvision, some resistance to damage, and an unsettling beauty that unnerves the living.
hud-feat-vampires_plaything_title = Vampire's Plaything
    .desc = The character has been marked as the property of a vampire lord — a dangerous status that grants them a measure of protection from lesser undead and the terrifying social authority of being associated with an immortal predator.
